From 8360a9aeef5380827d4703bcce587b424933dc70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 04:04:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 206/217] fix(execution): close U1 independent-review blockers

task=u1-matmul-policy-slice
review=independent-u1-review-3-blockers

- target probe: capability snapshots must match the probed local host
  (CapabilitySnapshot.probe_host / matches_host_probe); explicit policy
  targets are checked against the probe instead of being copied into a
  synthetic cpu snapshot. Fabricated triples (aarch64-linux-gnu, cuda-linux,
  riscv64-unknown, ...) now fail CAPABILITY_UNAVAILABLE before execution and
  can never run the portable CPU runtime under a false target.
- policy_from_dict: only schema_version == int(1) is accepted; missing,
  wrong-type or other values fail POLICY_INVALID_VALUE (no silent drop).
- alias safety: an output that is the same object as, or shares storage
  with, an input is rejected with OP_CONTRACT_INVALID before compile/launch;
  layout_decision.alias_check reports verified_distinct on success.
- hardening: artifact version declaration is validated before
  CpuScalarRuntime.launch (failures leave the output buffer untouched);
  policy/dtype error leaks are converted to structured execution errors;
  capability deterministic must be a real bool; provider required_features
  participate in candidate filtering; ExecutionPlan.validate type-checks
  shape/dtype/provider/artifact/fallback fields so malformed plans are
  rejected before any provider call.
- tests: 7 new regressions covering all three blockers and the hardening
  items (50 focused tests total).
